ted to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le08ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to tell a story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Regular verbs end in -ed or -ied.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": " Irregular verbs change in different ways."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to tell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"told\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to run\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ran\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to become\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"became\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to lose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lost\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to fall\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to slide\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"slid\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to begin\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"began\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She told me an interesting legend. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was about an elephant.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The elephant had a great fall."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past Time Expressions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about things that happened in the past, you can use a Past time expression.. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Here is a list of Past time expressions: <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Last (night/week/year) <li>This (week/year) <li>Many years/A long time ago <li>When ... was/were <li>Days/Weeks/Months passed <li>From that day/then on</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "A long time ago, in a far away place there lived a man ...  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Months passed, and the prince didn't come back. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "From that day on, it started to rain."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to frighten "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make someone or something feel afraid "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The animals became frightened."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a myth."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proud"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having respect for yourself "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He was too proud to leave."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to worry"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to think a lot about something you are scared about  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He was worried about what the queen would do."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob07aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "journey "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a period of time spent travelling from one place to another "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The snake started his long journey across the desert."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to beg "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to ask for something because you want it very much "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He begged the queen not to take away his powers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to promise "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to tell someone that you will do something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The snake promised to be kind."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to feel sorry for"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to feel pity for someone because they are in a bad situation "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He felt sorry for the lion and helped him."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take away"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to remove "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The evil queen took away his powers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pride "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a feeling that you like and respect yourself and that you deserve to be respected by other people "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: The father was full of pride as his child graduated."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le08ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brainstorm some ideas about how you think the snake lost its legs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose one idea. Write a short myth."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your myth."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give your myth to a partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read their myth."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your myths. What did you like? What was funny? Interesting?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I tell a story."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the Simple Past tense. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss with my partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le08ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le08ob07re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le08ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Long ago in Africa, the moon told the animals that there wouldn't be any rain that year. They became frightened and ran away but the snake didn't.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le08ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The snake had legs like the other animals. He was proud, and wanted to stay. \"I am not worried,\" he said.", "id": 2, "time": "10000", "image": "engenn5le08ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Days passed and still no rain. The snake decided it was time to leave. He began his journey through the desert. Soon, he was tired and couldn't walk anymore. He fell to his knees. He begged the moon to help him. He promised he would never be proud again. The moon looked down and felt sorry for him.", "id": 3, "time": "18500", "image": "engenn5le08ob07re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "She took away his legs, and he slid through the sand and crossed the desert.The snake never walked on two legs again, and from that day on he gave up his pride.", "id": 4, "time": "40000", "image": "engenn5le08ob07re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Vocabulary and Grammar"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can use past time expressions. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk or report about actions, events or people. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can tell a story."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What myths or legends about animals do you know?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are they about?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "What happened to the snake's legs?"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "resp